### WHAT AM I DOING?

    I am going to separate a single instance of a game into pieces.
    It is not a flawless approach but it is significantly more contextual than the alternative.

### HOW IS THAT WORKING?

    A game will be split into three. Early, mid, and late-game.
    Each lane has their own je ne sais quoi, but that is for a later stage of things. 
    Now I'll focus on mid lane as it is the "simplest" one.

### WHAT WILL THAT MEAN?

    I will still retrieve data through MATCH-V5, but that data will be stripped.
    Each game replay data will be turned into 3 files, one for each stage of the game.

## **STAGE ONE - EARLY-GAME** 

    Early game, as per my general game knowledge, composes the point where taking damage is the most.. damaging.
    CS, trades and kills are super important. Deaths will carry a really high penalty, aswell as cs disadvantages.
    An early-game winner is he who takes their turret or has a really high map impact.
    Kills outside their lane is considered map impact.
    Objectives outside their lane is considered map impact.

# **SUTEJI NI - MItsuDO GEEMU**

    Mid game is characterized mostly by skirmishes over map control and objectives.
    